Hi all,

My latest ascension - a wishless, atheist, weaponless, genoless,
polyselfless wizard. This was attempted as I've wanted to do a
wishless game for a while, as well as a weaponless character not a
monk. I then thought "hey, why not try for atheist as well"! Choose
wizard due to having poor combat skills to begin with, the spells
would be very nice for ranged attack in the early game, keeping
jackals, geckos and newts away! This wizard was not the first attempt
- countless others died due to either the monsters, or hunger due to
the increased spellcasting in the early game.

Started with a spellbook of light - one of my favourites, as it allows
easier passage through the dark Mines, and enchances Diviniation skill
for when I find Identify. Also a +2 ring of protection, and a magic
marker. The RNG obviously wanted me to make it past Dlvl 1 - a +5 ring
of protection and a suit of crystal plate mail meant I had an AC of -5
before going to lvl 2! Another nice find was the +oMagic Missile on
Dlvl 2 , and the wand of fire on Dlvl 3.

Went down to Sokoban first - this had the BoH, which was nice as I was
struggling to carry everything I wanted by this point. Minetown gave
me a magic lamp, which was used as a light source, and I managed to
collect 20 dagger in the mines which gave me something to use those ?
oEA on!

The Big Room had a bones pile of a previous wizard, which gave me
Sting, speed boots, a robe, holy water in a sack and a "oR. Things
were starting to look very hopeful for this wizard - at this point I
was Expert in dagger, had Magic Missile and Cone of Cold at 0% failure
and an AC of -10. My magic marker was used to write a +oID so I could
find out what some of these rings were. The only problem was, I
couldn't carry nearly as much as usual, I think because the crystal
plate mail was too heavy.

The Quest was fairly easy, just kept chucking +4 daggers at him until
he died. The Eye was very useful - I set up my stash level in Sokoban,
so I could teleport there from anywhere in the dungeon. The Castle and
Medusa were also fairly easy to clear out, only normal liches here.
Had to polypile spellbooks for magic mapping, detect treasure and dig.

Everything went fine until the way back up with the Amulet - 2 arch
liches appeared in Gehennom, and held me up for a long time, cursing a
lot of my stuff. Managed to dispose of them by teleporting to the
upstairs, then chucking daggers until they died. Made it though the
Plain of Air by casting Charm Monster on most of the elementals. Chose
to try the altar with Famine guarding it first - luckily this was the
right one.

